 13194139535414 true] [17592186348050 1089 "q-347466" 13194139535414 true] [17592186348050 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535414 true] [17592186348050 1100 "Find the second-degree Taylor polynomial ${P}_{2}(x)$ of $f(x)=\\frac{1}{1-\\sqrt{2}\\,x}$ about $x=0.$\n\n${P}_{2}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,+$\n{{field-2}}$\\,x\\,+$\n{{field-3}}$\\,{x}^{2}$" 13194139535414 true] [17592186348050 1113 #uuid "e0cf8efa-6fc7-5bd2-bd5d-4aeaac7ec023" 13194139535414 true] [17592186348050 1145 "To find the second-degree Taylor polynomial about $x=0,$ we plug $a=0$ into the general formula to give\n\n$$\n{P}_{2}(x)=f(0)+{f}^{′}(0)(x-0)+\\frac{1}{2}{f}^{″}(0)(x-0)^{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, we need to work out $f(0),$ ${f}^{′}(0),$ and ${f}^{″}(0):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{1}{1-\\sqrt{2}\\,x}=(1-\\sqrt{2}\\,x)^{-1} & ⟹ &  & f(0) & =1 \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =\\sqrt{2}(1-\\sqrt{2}\\,x)^{-2} & ⟹ &  & {f}^{′}(0) & =\\sqrt{2} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =4(1-\\sqrt{2}\\,x)^{-3} & ⟹ &  & {f}^{″}(0) & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now plug the results for $f(0),$ ${f}^{′}(0),$ and ${f}^{″}(0)$ into our second-degree Taylor polynomial. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{2}(x) & =1+\\sqrt{2}\\,x+4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2} \\\\  & =1+\\sqrt{2}\\,x+2\\,{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535414 true] [17592186348051 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348052 13194139535414 true] [17592186348051 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535414 true] [17592186348051 1041 "field-1" 13194139535414 true] [17592186348051 1104 #edb/ref 17592186348052 13194139535414 true] [17592186348051 1110 #uuid "078a3e91-6106-5938-859d-451323231709" 13194139535414 true] [17592186348052 1034 "1" 13194139535414 true] [17592186348052 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535414 true] [17592186348052 1111 #uuid "b314e82c-c376-5f16-a296-e0f1868064c1" 13194139535414 true] [17592186348053 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348054 13194139535414 true] [17592186348053 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535414 true] [17592186348053 1041 "field-2" 13194139535414 true